# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SETUP - ENSURE TEST ACCOUNTS EXIST
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Provisions the shared ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_EMAIL/PASSWORD account that every other suite logs in as
# "the plain mechanic" (tests/API/admin/*.http, tests/API/authz/mechanic-forbidden.http, and the
# Python checks' http_check_support.read_credentials), so a fresh or drifted database always has an
# account to authenticate against.
#
# Ordering caveat (verified, not assumed): the runner invokes
# `npx httpyac tests/API/**/*.http --all ...` (scripts/run-local-test-suite.py), and httpyac resolves
# that glob through `globby(pattern, { gitignore: true })` (confirmed by reading the bundled
# httpyac/dist/index.js). Probing globby directly with the exact same pattern and cwd from a Node
# REPL, repeated eight times, showed the cross-directory order is NOT stable run to run - even which
# top-level folder comes first varied between runs (fast-glob/fdir walks sibling directories
# concurrently and appends results as each directory's read settles). So "_setup" sorting before
# "admin" alphabetically does not guarantee httpyac resolves it first on every run, and no folder
# name can guarantee that under this mechanism. This file is written to not depend on running first:
# the registration call below tolerates the account already existing (see its comment), and the
# actual invariant this file protects - the account being usable - is proven by the login assertion
# at the end. Once created, the account persists across runs (the API only reseeds the three
# built-in demo mechanics' passwords on start, per Data/DemoDataInitializer.cs), so any run where
# this file happens to execute after a file that needed the account self-heals on the next run.
#
# If the account already exists with a DIFFERENT password than ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_PASSWORD (created
# by hand, or by an older fixture), the login below fails with 401 and the owner must fix the local
# tests/.env to match the real stored password - this file never attempts to reset it.

@AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress = {{$processEnv AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}
@WebUI_Origin = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_WEBUI_ORIGIN}}
@AdminEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_EMAIL}}
@AdminPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_ADMIN_PASSWORD}}
@MechanicEmail = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_EMAIL}}
@MechanicPassword = {{$processEnv ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_PASSWORD}}


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [Setup] Clear any session cookie left by a previous file (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup] Probe the plain mechanic test login (not asserted - the repair step below decides)
# @name mechanicProbe
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{MechanicEmail}}",
  "password": "{{MechanicPassword}}"
}

###

### [Setup] Clear the probe session before the admin login (204 or 401, not asserted)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}

###

### [Setup] Login as admin to provision the shared plain-mechanic test account (200 expected)
# @name Login
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{AdminEmail}}",
  "password": "{{AdminPassword}}"
}

{{
  exports.CsrfToken = response.headers['set-cookie']?.find(c => c.startsWith('autoservice_csrf='))?.match(/^autoservice_csrf=([^;]+)/)?.[1];
}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup] List mechanics to find a stale plain-mechanic test account (200 expected)
# @name allMechanics
GET {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/admin/mechanics

?? status == 200

###

### [Repair] Delete the plain mechanic test account only when its login failed (200 expected per delete)
# Self-healing (user decision 2026-09-27): an earlier, non-idempotent password-change test could leave
# this account with a password that no longer matches ARSM_TEST_MECHANIC_PASSWORD, and every later
# plain-mechanic case then fails with 401. When the probe login above did not return a personId, the
# account is deleted here and re-registered below with the configured password. Strictly limited to an
# '@example.test' address that is not an admin - a demo '@example.com' account is never touched (the API
# re-seeds those on start). The loop runs zero times when the probe succeeded.
# @loop for staleMechanic of (mechanicProbe && mechanicProbe.personId ? [] : allMechanics.filter(m => !m.isAdmin && m.email.toLowerCase() === MechanicEmail.toLowerCase() && m.email.toLowerCase().endsWith("@example.test")))
DELETE {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/admin/mechanics/{{staleMechanic.personId}}
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 200

###

### [Setup] Register the plain mechanic test account if it does not already exist
# AuthEndpoints.Register (AdminOnly, verified in AuthEndpoints.Register.cs) answers 200 OK with
# { personId, personType, email } for a fresh account, or 400 ValidationProblem with a generic
# "register" field error for ANY conflict (duplicate email, duplicate phone, or a unique-constraint
# race) - the same message regardless of cause, by design, to avoid account enumeration. Both are the
# correct outcome here depending on whether an earlier run already created this account, so this
# asserts the precise pair of allowed codes rather than a vague range.
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/register
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "firstName": "Test",
  "lastName": "Mechanic",
  "email": "{{MechanicEmail}}",
  "password": "{{MechanicPassword}}",
  "personType": "Mechanic",
  "specialization": "GasolineAndDiesel",
  "expertise": ["Engine", "Brakes"]
}

?? js [200, 400].includes(response.statusCode) == true

###

### [Setup] Logout admin before proving the plain-mechanic account can log in (204 expected)
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/logout
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{CsrfToken}}

?? status == 204

###

### [Positive] Plain mechanic test account logs in (200 expected)
# After the repair step this succeeds for an '@example.test' account. A 401 that remains means the account
# is a demo '@example.com' mechanic (never reset here) or could not be deleted (e.g. 422 sole appointment
# assignee): fix tests/.env to match the stored password.
POST {{AutoService_ApiService_HostAddress}}/api/auth/login
Origin: {{WebUI_Origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{MechanicEmail}}",
  "password": "{{MechanicPassword}}"
}

?? status == 200
